# REQUIRES: verilator
# (11-08: the runs pin --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct, the defaults before then, so that the
# link counts and registers checked below stay those of the feature under test.)
# HBM link streams (`--link-kinds <producer>:<reader>:hbm`): the early links
# from one producer class to one reader class kept in device memory behind a
# virtual memory of one image (INSTANCES 1), a row a single address, the
# request's tag a landing slot. The producer's bits the links read are held
# at its pass and written a row a host cycle after it; each reader pass's
# rows (Reader reads two Units' rows: two landings a pass) are requested
# `lead` positions ahead and land over the host cycles before its slot, a
# bubble where a landing's response is late. Exact against the target
# (Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv: the virtual memories' model, rows zero at start,
# answered 1 to 60 host cycles on, `free` low at times), channels stalled or
# not, with bubbles; one stream alone; and the report's stream lines.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/linkhbm
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/two --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm Unit Reader 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TWO
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VH < %t/two/foldsim_sim.vh
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/two -DVM1 -Mdir %t/two/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/two/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/two/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/two/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/two/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=20 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/two/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+4 +lo=1 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/bub --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --bubbles --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm Unit Reader > %t/bub.log 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/bub -DVM1 -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/bub/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/bub/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/bub/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/bub/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+5 +bubble=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/bub/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+6 +bubble=30 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=30 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# link-hbm-beat-bits: a row wider than 16 bits (32) moves as 2 beats of a
# 16-bit controller where the landings and the producer's passes leave the
# positions (a frame of 256): the beats' requests before the landing's, the
# slot written beat by beat; exact with bubbles, stalls and long latencies.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/beat --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --bubbles --min-ii 256 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm --link-hbm-beat-bits 16 Unit Reader > %t/beat.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BEATVH < %t/beat/foldsim_sim.vh
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/beat -DVM1 -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/beat/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/beat/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/beat/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/beat/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+5 +bubble=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/beat/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+6 +bubble=30 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=30 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/beat/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+7 +lo=1 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# BEATVH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_DW 16
# Three beats (--link-hbm-beat-bits 11: 16-bit beats of a 32-bit row) on the
# stream's own virtual memory: a slot's pending beats at a stride of 4 bits
# (as {slot, beat} indexes them; at 3 a slot's last beat fell in the next
# slot's bits and a slot read as landed early: MISMATCH at +hi=60 before).
# Exact with long latencies, bubbles and stalls.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/beat3v --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --bubbles --min-ii 256 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm --link-hbm-beat-bits 11 Unit Reader > %t/beat3v.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BEATVH < %t/beat3v/foldsim_sim.vh
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/beat3v -DVM1 -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/beat3v/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/beat3v/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/beat3v/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/beat3v/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+7 +lo=1 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/beat3v/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+9 +lo=1 +hi=600 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/beat3v/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+8 +bubble=50 +stall=50 +lo=1 +hi=600 +full=30 | FileCheck %s
# The same on page engines (--page-engines): the beat stream's engine 16 bits
# wide; its requests and writes may move by a constant (the first engine
# they fit). Exact.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/beateng --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --bubbles --min-ii 256 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm --link-hbm-beat-bits 16 --page-engines 4 Unit Reader > %t/beateng.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BEATENG < %t/beateng/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/beateng -DVM1 -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/beateng/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/beateng/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/beateng/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/beateng/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+6 +bubble=30 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=30 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/beateng/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+7 +lo=1 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# BEATENG: page engine {{[0-9]+}} 16 bits
# Three beats of 16 bits for a 32-bit row (--link-hbm-beat-bits 11): the beat
# select has a fourth, zero entry, indexed while no write leaves, so the
# stream's write data and mask are zero while idle and its engine takes them
# without a select of its own (zero idle). Exact with bubbles, stalls and long
# latencies.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/beat3 --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --bubbles --min-ii 256 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm --link-hbm-beat-bits 11 --page-engines 4 Unit Reader > %t/beat3.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BEAT3 < %t/beat3/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/beat3 -DVM1 -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/beat3/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/beat3/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/beat3/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/beat3/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+5 +bubble=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/beat3/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+6 +bubble=30 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=30 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/beat3/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+7 +lo=1 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/beat3/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+8 +bubble=50 +stall=50 +lo=1 +hi=600 +full=30 | FileCheck %s
# BEAT3: page engine {{[0-9]+}} 16 bits, {{.*}} link:Reader>Unit(zero idle)
# BEAT3: page engine {{[0-9]+}} 32 bits, {{.*}} link:Unit>Reader{{$}}
# --link-hbm-beat-rows: a stream of beats lands in rows of a beat ({slot,
# beat}: 128 x 16 bits, not 64 x 32 with a beat mask), read beat by beat into
# its members' registers from the position before its landing's. With 2 beats
# the Units' landings, 3 apart, are just far enough (beats + 1: the first beat
# loads the registers at the pass that reads the landing before); with 3
# beats they are not, and that stream keeps its whole-row landing. Exact with
# bubbles, stalls and long latencies, on its own memory and on an engine.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/rows2 --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --bubbles --min-ii 256 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm --link-hbm-beat-bits 16 --link-hbm-beat-rows Unit Reader > %t/rows2.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ROWS2 < %t/rows2/schedule.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ROWS2M < %t/rows2/foldsim_sim.mlir
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/rows2 -DVM1 -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/rows2/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/rows2/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/rows2/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/rows2/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+5 +bubble=30 | FileCheck %s
