# ROWS3: link-hbm beat rows: 0 of 1 streams of beats
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/one --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --link-kinds Reader:Unit:hbm Unit Reader > %t/one.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ONE < %t/one/schedule.txt
# A shorter lead (--link-hbm-lead): requests 10 positions ahead (the fewest: the decisions in flight + 6), more bubbles, as exact.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/lead --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --link-hbm-lead 10 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm Unit Reader > %t/lead.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LEAD < %t/lead/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/lead -DVM1 -Mdir %t/lead/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/lead/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/lead/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/lead/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+3 +lo=8 +hi=40 | FileCheck %s
# --link-hbm-min-lead: a member with less room from its row's write to its
# landing than that is an on-chip link (its landing would wait for the
# memory's round trip every frame): of Unit -> Reader's two members, the one
# with room 10 stays on chip at 11, and the stream's lead is the other's.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/minl --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --link-hbm-min-lead 11 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm Unit Reader > %t/minl.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MINL < %t/minl/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/minl -DVM1 -Mdir %t/minl/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/minl/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/minl/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/minl/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+7 +lo=1 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# A stream none of whose members is kept builds nothing, so its ports space
# no pass: it is excluded and the frame scheduled again without it. At 100
# no member has the room: both streams excluded, the frame the stream-free
# fold's (no hbm rule; before, II 64 against 16: the dropped streams' ports
# still spaced the passes), every link on chip, exact. At 20 Reader -> Unit
# keeps none: excluded, and Unit -> Reader's members planned anew on the
# frame without its spacing (both kept, lead 40), exact.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/free --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo Unit Reader > %t/free.log 2>&1
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/drop --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --link-hbm-min-lead 100 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm Unit Reader > %t/drop.log 2>&1
# RUN: cat %t/free.log %t/drop.log | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DROP
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DROPX < %t/drop.log
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/drop/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/drop/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/drop/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/drop/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/drop/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/drop1 --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --link-hbm-min-lead 20 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm Unit Reader 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DROP1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/drop1 -Mdir %t/drop1/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/drop1/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/drop1/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/drop1/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+3 +lo=1 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/drop1/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+4 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=20 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# DROP: II = [[II:[0-9]+]]{{$}}
# DROP: II = [[II]]{{$}}
# DROP: link streams: 0 streams, 0 links, 0 bits
# DROPX: link stream Reader -> Unit keeps no member
# DROPX: link stream Unit -> Reader keeps no member
# DROP1: link stream Reader -> Unit keeps no member
# DROP1-NOT: Unit -> Reader keeps no member
# DROP1: link streams: 1 streams, 2 links
# DROP1: link stream Unit Reader 2 0 32 32 1 16 32 2 40{{$}}
# --link-hbm-row-bits: a stream's row (its controller's data width) at most
# that many bits; a wider word is cut into rows, written one a host cycle
# after the producer's pass and landing one a host cycle before the
# reader's (16: two rows a 32-bit word, the passes spaced, a longer frame).
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/rowb --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --link-hbm-row-bits 16 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm Unit Reader > %t/rowb.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ROWB < %t/rowb/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/rowb -DVM1 -Mdir %t/rowb/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/rowb/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/rowb/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/rowb/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 +lo=1 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/rowb/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=20 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: not foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/rowbad --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --link-hbm-row-bits 5000 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm Unit Reader 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ROWBAD
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/one -Mdir %t/one/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/one/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/one/build.log 2>&1
